{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000080:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a16537ae4276ed87940a001d10d1fa\",\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-13-1\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"\\\\r\\\\n    \\\\\\\"skills\\\\\\\": [\\\\r\\\\n      {\\\\r\\\\n>       \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"taste-design\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n>       \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"taste-design\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n>       \\\\\\\"display_name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"taste-design\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n        \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Apply distinctive, anti-generic visual taste to web frontend design, redesign, and polish work.\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n        \\\\\\\"short_description\\\\\\\": null,\\\\r\\\\n          \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"local\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\n        },\\\\r\\\\n>       \\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"$CONFIG_DIR/skills/taste-design/SKILL.md\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n        \\\\\\\"activation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"on\\\\\\\",\\\\r\\\\n        \\\\\\\"diagnostics\\\\\\\": [],\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 453,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 114,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\"}","truncated":false}
{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"bfbc2997-1ece-459a-822e-8e6119964510:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"assistant","source":"tool_call","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_call\",\"id\":\"fc_01a16532946c74b2b63026d50153c8ad\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a16532946c74b2b63026d50153c8ad\",\"name\":\"write_file\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\danie\\\\\\\\OneDrive\\\\\\\\github-repos\\\\\\\\.agents\\\\\\\\skill-drafts\\\\\\\\taste-design\\\\\\\\SKILL.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"---\\\\nname: taste-design\\\\ndescription: Apply distinctive, anti-generic visual taste to web frontend design, redesign, and polish work.\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Taste Design\\\\n\\\\nUse this skill whenever you design, build, redesign, or polish a web page,\\\\ncomponent, app screen, dashboard, landing page, or portfolio. It is only\\\\nabout visual taste and design quality. It does not replace project\\\\nrequirements, accessibility rules, or an existing design system.\\\\n\\\\n## Goal\\\\n\\\\nProduce an interface that looks intentionally art-directed for its subject,\\\\nnot like a generic AI template. Make one clear visual idea obvious at first\\\\nglance, then keep every detail consistent with it.\\\\n\\\\n## Dials\\\\n\\\\nSet these before coding. State them in one line in your working notes.\\\\n\\\\n- `DESIGN_VARIANCE` (1-10, default 7): layout experimentation. Low is\\\\n  conventional and symmetric; high is editorial, offset, and asymmetric.\\\\n- `MOTION_INTENSITY` (1-10, default 4): animation depth. Low is hover-only;\\\\n  mid is entrances and state transitions; high is scroll-linked motion.\\\\n  Never add motion the user did not ask for to a static object.\\\\n- `VISUAL_DENSITY` (1-10, default 4): information per viewport. Low is\\\\n  spacious and gallery-like; high is dense and operational.\\\\n\\\\nRaise variance for marketing, portfolio, and editorial pages. Lower variance\\\\nand raise density for dashboards, tools, and admin screens. Respect an\\\\nexisting design system over these defaults.\\\\n\\\\n## Before Writing Code\\\\n\\\\nCommit to an art direction in four decisions:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Concept**: name the one signature idea in a short phrase, for example\\\\n   \\\\\\\"field-notes journal\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"precision instrument\\\\\\\", or \\\\\\\"quiet gallery\\\\\\\".\\\\n2. **Typography**: pick a display voice and a text voice. Use a real type\\\\n   scale with strong contrast between headline, body, and caption sizes.\\\\n3. **Color**: pick a dominant surface, one ink color, and one accent.\\\\n   Derive tints and shades from those. No default palette.\\\\n4. **Layout**: decide the grid, the asymmetry, and where the eye lands\\\\n   first, second, and third.\\\\n\\\\nIf the brief is vague, choose a direction that fits the subject matter\\\\ninstead of asking the user to art-direct it.\\\\n\\\\n## Design Rules\\\\n\\\\n- Lead with hierarchy: one dominant element per view, then supporting\\\\n  elements clearly smaller, quieter, or further away.\\\\n- Use spacing as structure. Group with generous gaps between sections and\\\\n  tight gaps inside groups. Keep a consistent spacing rhythm.\\\\n- Prefer editorial composition: offset blocks, overlapping layers, wide\\\\n  margins, oversized numerals or headlines, and left-aligned text over\\\\n  centered stacks.\\\\n- Give typography the main job. Tight tracking on large headlines, relaxed\\\\n  line-height on body text, uppercase micro-labels only where useful.\\\\n- Use imagery, texture, borders, and shadows to create depth with intent.\\\\n  Every decorative element must support the concept.\\\\n- Design all states: hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, empty, and\\\\n  error. A screen with only a happy path is unfinished.\\\\n- Keep motion purposeful: it reveals hierarchy, confirms an action, or\\\\n  guides the eye. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\\\\n- Keep accessibility intact: sufficient contrast, visible focus, semantic\\\\n  structure, and targets at least 44px where practical.\\\\n\\\\n## Banned Defaults\\\\n\\\\nDo not ship these unless the concept explicitly calls for them:\\\\n\\\\n- Purple or blue gradient hero with centered headline and two buttons.\\\\n- Uniform rounded cards with soft shadows in an equal grid.\\\\n- Glassmorphism, glow, and blur used as decoration without purpose.\\\\n- Default sans-serif everywhere with no display voic…","truncated":true}
